## Context

`erg init` unpacks two embedded assets into a store: `tickets/.ergrc` and
`tickets/AGENTS.md` (see `src/go/init.go:11-12`). The "init-unpacked AGENTS.md
contains non-ASCII or non-printable bytes" guard in `tests/test_init.sh:149`
checks only `AGENTS.md`. `.ergrc` is unpacked the same way but goes unchecked,
so a non-ASCII byte introduced into `src/go/assets/.ergrc` ships silently.

Surfaced while fixing PR #305 (ticket 0244): a Unicode em-dash slipped into the
AGENTS.md asset and the guard caught it. The same mistake in `.ergrc` would
not be caught. `.ergrc` is ASCII today -- this is a guard gap, not a live bug.

## Relevant files
- `tests/test_init.sh` (~line 149) -- the single-file ASCII assertion
- `src/go/init.go` (lines 11-12) -- the list of unpacked assets

## Actions
1. Generalize the guard to assert pure ASCII / printable bytes over **every**
   unpacked asset, ideally by iterating the same file list `init` uses rather
   than naming each by hand (so a future third asset is covered automatically).

## Test
- Red step: a deliberate non-ASCII byte in `src/go/assets/.ergrc` must make
  `test_init.sh` fail before the guard is generalized.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The ASCII/printable guard covers `tickets/.ergrc` as well as `AGENTS.md`
- [ ] A non-ASCII byte in either unpacked asset fails `make test`
- [ ] `make test` green on the clean tree
